{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4dd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08787-bf24-7b40-897c-97ffe37e976a"},"sequence":201,"recorded_at":1780531400000397,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137"},"call_id":"call_01a0878825ad7881973161df39c9d499","text":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/query.go`.\n1|// Package sessquery composes the session repository and state projector for\n2|// read-only NAME/UUID resolution and local list/status summaries. It implements\n3|// the specified portions of TASK-260830-21gygk against SPEC v0.5.0 Sections 2.3,\n4|// 5.1–5.2, 5.7 and 14.4. It defines no qualified-selector grammar or action route.\n5|package sessquery\n6|\n7|import (\n8|\t\"errors\"\n9|\t\"fmt\"\n10|\t\"sort\"\n11|\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessstate\"\n15|)\n16|\n17|var (\n18|\tErrUnavailable = errors.New(\"session index unavailable\")\n19|\tErrAmbiguous   = sessrepo.ErrNameAmbiguous\n20|\tErrNotFound    = sessrepo.ErrNameNotFound\n21|)\n22|\n23|// PeerIndex binds a peer identity to its already persisted learned index.\n24|// Transport/authentication and installing peer indexes are upstream owners;\n25|// this reader does not fetch, authenticate, or attest a caller-supplied index.\n26|type PeerIndex struct {\n27|\tHostID string\n28|\tRepo   *sessrepo.Repository\n29|}\n30|\n31|// Reader reads existing indexes. AllowlistedPeerIDs must come from the owning\n32|// configuration layer, separately from the learned indexes. An unlisted source\n33|// is never read. Failed reads from listed sources are errors, never\n34|// empty indexes that let resolution fall through to a lower-priority UUID.\n35|// LocalHostID comes from the local host identity owner; empty preserves unknown.\n36|type Reader struct {\n37|\tLocal              *sessrepo.Repository\n38|\tLocalHostID        string\n39|\tAllowlistedPeerIDs []string\n40|\tPeers              []PeerIndex\n41|}\n42|\n43|// Summary contains only facts derived from verified session records and events.\n44|// It is an internal read model, not the closed Section 14.2 CLI SessionSummary.\n45|// Unknown owner/lease and parked diagnostics remain explicit in Projection.\n46|// Host display names, checkpoint timestamps/age, workspace state, capabilities,\n47|// process liveness and sync timestamps require their respective observation\n48|// owners and are deliberately not inferred from a record or a successful read.\n49|type Summary struct {\n50|\tProjection sessstate.Projection\n51|}\n52|\n53|// List reads local summaries in bytewise session-ID order. Parked sessions stay\n54|// visible with their blocking reason and retry; failure to enumerate the index\n55|// fails the read. No durable state is written, even for an interrupted create.\n56|func (reader *Reader) List() ([]Summary, error) {\n57|\tif reader == nil || reader.Local == nil {\n58|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local repository is required\", ErrUnavailable)\n59|\t}\n60|\treturn reader.read(reader.Local)\n61|}\n62|\n63|func (reader *Reader) read(repo *sessrepo.Repository) ([]Summary, error) {\n64|\trows, err := repo.ListSessions()\n65|\tif err != nil {\n66|\t\treturn nil, err\n67|\t}\n68|\tout := make([]Summary, 0, len(rows))\n69|\tprojector := sessstate.Projector{Repo: repo, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}\n70|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n71|\t\tprojection, err := projector.Project(row.SessionID)\n72|\t\tif err != nil {\n73|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n74|\t\t}\n75|\t\tout = append(out, Summary{Projection: projection})\n76|\t}\n77|\tsort.Slice(out, func(i, j int) bool { return out[i].Projection.SessionID < out[j].Projection.SessionID })\n78|\treturn out, nil\n79|}\n80|\n81|// Status resolves a NAME/UUID through the same path as Resolve, then projects\n82|// from the selected repository. It never treats a failed read as not found.\n83|// Parked sessions can be inspected by ID through InspectLocal, independently of\n84|// live-name routing, so operators retain access to the recovery diagnostics.\n85|func (reader *Reader) Status(selector string) (Summary, error) {\n86|\tselected, err := reader.Resolve(selector)\n87|\tif err != nil {\n88|\t\treturn Summary{}, err\n89|\t}\n90|\tprojection, err := (&sessstate.Projector{Repo: selected.repo, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}).Project(selected.SessionID)\n91|\tif err != nil {\n92|\t\treturn Summary{}, err\n93|\t}\n94|\treturn Summary{Projection: projection}, nil\n95|}\n96|\n97|// InspectLocal reads one local ID, including a parked or tombstoned session.\n98|func (reader *Reader) InspectLocal(sessionID string) (Summary, error) {\n99|\tif reader == nil || reader.Local == nil {\n100|\t\treturn Summary{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local repository is required\", ErrUnavailable)\n101|\t}\n102|\tprojection, err := (&sessstate.Projector{Repo: reader.Local, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}).Project(sessionID)\n103|\tif err != nil {\n104|\t\treturn Summary{}, err\n105|\t}\n106|\treturn Summary{Projection: projection}, nil\n107|}\n108|\n109|// Selection identifies the session and source index, never an attach or mutation\n110|// plan. PeerHostID is empty for local resolution; it is not the winning owner.\n111|type Selection struct {\n112|\tSessionID  string\n113|\tPeerHostID string\n114|\trepo       *sessrepo.Repository\n115|}\n116|\n117|type candidate struct {\n118|\tsummary   Summary\n119|\tselection Selection\n120|}\n121|\n122|// Resolve applies the Section 2.3 tiers: local exact live name, allowlisted\n123|// peer exact live name, exact UUID, not found. ASCII folding detects collisions\n124|// within each name tier; it does not turn a unique case variant into an exact\n125|// match. Repository-parked and tombstoned entries are not live-name candidates.\n126|// This is logical index eligibility, not proof of process liveness or safe\n127|// attach/resume readiness; those decisions belong to the action planner.\n128|func (reader *Reader) Resolve(selector string) (Selection, error) {\n129|\tlocal, err := reader.List()\n130|\tif err != nil {\n131|\t\treturn Selection{}, err\n132|\t}\n133|\tcandidates := liveCandidates(local, reader.Local, \"\")\n134|\tif match, found, err := matchName(candidates, selector); found || err != nil {\n135|\t\treturn match, err\n136|\t}\n137|\tpeers, err := reader.peerCandidates()\n138|\tif err != nil {\n139|\t\treturn Selection{}, err\n140|\t}\n141|\tif match, found, err := matchName(peers, selector); found || err != nil {\n142|\t\treturn match, err\n143|\t}\n144|\tif id, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(selector); err == nil {\n145|\t\tfor _, item := range append(candidates, peers...) {\n146|\t\t\tif item.selection.SessionID == id.String() {\n147|\t\t\t\treturn item.selection, nil\n148|\t\t\t}\n149|\t\t}\n150|\t}\n151|\treturn Selection{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: no live session named %q\", ErrNotFound, selector)\n152|}\n153|\n154|func liveCandidates(rows []Summary, repo *sessrepo.Repository, peer string) []candidate {\n155|\tout := make([]candidate, 0, len(rows))\n156|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n157|\t\tif row.Projection.Parked != nil || row.Projection.State == sessstate.StateTombstoned {\n158|\t\t\tcontinue\n159|\t\t}\n160|\t\tout = append(out, candidate{row, Selection{row.Projection.SessionID, peer, repo}})\n161|\t}\n162|\treturn out\n163|}\n164|\n165|func (reader *Reader) peerCandidates() ([]candidate, error) {\n166|\tids := append([]string(nil), reader.AllowlistedPeerIDs...)\n167|\tsort.Strings(ids)\n168|\tvar out []candidate\n169|\tfor index, id := range ids {\n170|\t\tif index > 0 && id == ids[index-1] {\n171|\t\t\tcontinue\n172|\t\t}\n173|\t\tvar repo *sessrepo.Repository\n174|\t\tfound := false\n175|\t\tfor _, peer := range reader.Peers {\n176|\t\t\tif peer.HostID != id {\n177|\t\t\t\tcontinue\n178|\t\t\t}\n179|\t\t\tif found {\n180|\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: multiple indexes for peer %s\", ErrUnavailable, id)\n181|\t\t\t}\n182|\t\t\tfound = true\n183|\t\t\trepo = peer.Repo\n184|\t\t}\n185|\t\t// An allowlisted peer with no learned index contributes no learned names.\n186|\t\t// A listed index with an unavailable repository is a failed observation.\n187|\t\tif !found {\n188|\t\t\tcontinue\n189|\t\t}\n190|\t\tif repo == nil {\n191|\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: unreadable index for peer %s\", ErrUnavailable, id)\n192|\t\t}\n193|\t\trows, err := reader.read(repo)\n194|\t\tif err != nil {\n195|\t\t\treturn nil, err\n196|\t\t}\n197|\t\tout = append(out, liveCandidates(rows, repo, id)...)\n198|\t}\n199|\treturn out, nil\n200|}\n201|\n202|func matchName(items []candidate, selector string) (Selection, bool, error) {\n203|\t// A replicated session is one identity, regardless of how many peers learned\n204|\t// it. Distinct session IDs in the folded bucket are an ambiguity.\n205|\tids := make(map[string]struct{})\n206|\tvar exact *Selection\n207|\tfor _, item := range items {\n208|\t\tif asciiFold(item.summary.Projection.Name) != asciiFold(selector) {\n209|\t\t\tcontinue\n210|\t\t}\n211|\t\tids[item.selection.SessionID] = struct{}{}\n212|\t\tif item.summary.Projection.Name == selector && exact == nil {\n213|\t\t\tselection := item.selection\n214|\t\t\texact = &selection\n215|\t\t}\n216|\t}\n217|\tif len(ids) > 1 {\n218|\t\treturn Selection{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: name %q collides across %d sessions\", ErrAmbiguous, selector, len(ids))\n219|\t}\n220|\tif exact != nil {\n221|\t\treturn *exact, true, nil\n222|\t}\n223|\treturn Selection{}, false, nil\n224|}\n225|\n226|func asciiFold(value string) string {\n227|\tfolded := []byte(value)\n228|\tfor index, character := range folded {\n229|\t\tif character >= 'A' && character <= 'Z' {\n230|\t\t\tfolded[index] += 'a' - 'A'\n231|\t\t}\n232|\t}\n233|\treturn string(folded)\n234|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4df","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08787-bf24-7b40-897c-97ffe37e976a"},"sequence":202,"recorded_at":1780531400000399,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137"},"call_id":"call_01a08788264170c1bcf695d53a1e641a","text":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/query_test.go`.\n1|package sessquery\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\t\"os\"\n6|\t\"path/filepath\"\n7|\t\"reflect\"\n8|\t\"testing\"\n9|\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessstate\"\n12|)\n13|\n14|func TestResolvePinnedPrecedence(t *testing.T) {\n15|\tlocal, _ := repository(t)\n16|\tpeer, _ := repository(t)\n17|\tcreate(t, local, idA, \"Local\")\n18|\tcreate(t, peer, idB, idA)\n19|\treader := &Reader{Local: local, AllowlistedPeerIDs: []string{hostA}, Peers: []PeerIndex{{hostA, peer}}}\n20|\tfor _, row := range []struct{ selector, id, peer string }{\n21|\t\t{\"Local\", idA, \"\"}, {idA, idB, hostA}, {idB, idB, hostA},\n22|\t} {\n23|\t\tgot, err := reader.Resolve(row.selector)\n24|\t\tif err != nil || got.SessionID != row.id || got.PeerHostID != row.peer {\n25|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Resolve(%q) = %+v, %v\", row.selector, got, err)\n26|\t\t}\n27|\t\tstatus, err := reader.Status(row.selector)\n28|\t\tif err != nil || status.Projection.SessionID != row.id {\n29|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"Status(%q) = %+v, %v\", row.selector, status, err)\n30|\t\t}\n31|\t}\n32|\t// Local exact name wins even if a peer learned the same name for another ID.\n33|\tother, _ := repository(t)\n34|\tcreate(t, other, idB, \"Local\")\n35|\treader.Peers = []PeerIndex{{hostA, other}}\n36|\tgot, err := reader.Resolve(\"Local\")\n37|\tif err != nil || got.SessionID != idA || got.PeerHostID != \"\" {\n38|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"local priority: %+v %v\", got, err)\n39|\t}\n40|\t// A local UUID-shaped name also wins over the UUID identity.\n41|\tlocal2, _ := repository(t)\n42|\tcreate(t, local2, idA, \"Original\")\n43|\tcreate(t, local2, idB, idA)\n44|\tgot, err = (&Reader{Local: local2}).Resolve(idA)\n45|\tif err != nil || got.SessionID != idB {\n46|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"local name before UUID: %+v %v\", got, err)\n47|\t}\n48|}\n49|\n50|func TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions(t *testing.T) {\n51|\tfor _, peers := range []bool{false, true} {\n52|\t\tt.Run(map[bool]string{false: \"local\", true: \"peers\"}[peers], func(t *testing.T) {\n53|\t\t\tlocal, _ := repository(t)\n54|\t\t\tsource := local\n55|\t\t\tr := &Reader{Local: local}\n56|\t\t\tif peers {\n57|\t\t\t\tsource, _ = repository(t)\n58|\t\t\t\tr.AllowlistedPeerIDs = []string{hostA}\n59|\t\t\t\tr.Peers = []PeerIndex{{hostA, source}}\n60|\t\t\t}\n61|\t\t\tcreate(t, source, idA, \"Az-09._\")\n62|\t\t\tfor _, query := range []string{\"az-09._\", \"AZ-09._\", \"Ａz-09._\", \"no-such-session\", \"Name@host\", \"host/Name\", \"\"} {\n63|\t\t\t\tif _, err := r.Resolve(query); !errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound) {\n64|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%q: %v\", query, err)\n65|\t\t\t\t}\n66|\t\t\t}\n67|\t\t\tif _, err := r.Resolve(\"Az-09._\"); err != nil {\n68|\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n69|\t\t\t}\n70|\t\t\tcreate(t, source, idB, \"aZ-09._\")\n71|\t\t\tfor _, query := range []string{\"Az-09._\", \"aZ-09._\", \"AZ-09._\"} {\n72|\t\t\t\tif _, err := r.Resolve(query); !errors.Is(err, ErrAmbiguous) {\n73|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%q: %v\", query, err)\n74|\t\t\t\t}\n75|\t\t\t\tif _, err := r.Status(query); !errors.Is(err, ErrAmbiguous) {\n76|\t\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"status %q: %v\", query, err)\n77|\t\t\t\t}\n78|\t\t\t}\n79|\t\t})\n80|\t}\n81|}\n82|\n83|func TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures(t *testing.T) {\n84|\tlocal, root := repository(t)\n85|\tpeer, peerRoot := repository(t)\n86|\tcreate(t, local, idA, \"Local\")\n87|\tcreate(t, peer, idB, idA)\n88|\tr := &Reader{Local: local, Peers: []PeerIndex{{hostA, peer}}}\n89|\tgot, err := r.Resolve(idA)\n90|\tif err != nil || got.SessionID != idA {\n91|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"unallowlisted peer affected UUID: %+v %v\", got, err)\n92|\t}\n93|\t// No learned index is absence; a known index whose read fails is not.\n94|\tr.AllowlistedPeerIDs = []string{hostB}\n95|\tgot, err = r.Resolve(idA)\n96|\tif err != nil || got.SessionID != idA {\n97|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"absent learned index: %+v %v\", got, err)\n98|\t}\n99|\tr.AllowlistedPeerIDs = []string{hostA}\n100|\tif err := os.Rename(filepath.Join(peerRoot, \"sessions\"), filepath.Join(peerRoot, \"saved\")); err != nil {\n101|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n102|\t}\n103|\tif _, err := r.Resolve(idA); !errors.Is(err, sessrepo.ErrRepositoryPath) {\n104|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"failed peer read fell through: %v\", err)\n105|\t}\n106|\t// Local exact name does not depend on lower-tier reads.\n107|\tif _, err := r.Resolve(\"Local\"); err != nil {\n108|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n109|\t}\n110|\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(peerRoot, \"sessions\"), []byte(\"not a directory\"), 0600); err != nil {\n111|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n112|\t}\n113|\tif _, err := r.Status(idA); !errors.Is(err, sessrepo.ErrRepositoryPath) {\n114|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"non-directory read: %v\", err)\n115|\t}\n116|\tr.Peers = []PeerIndex{{hostA, nil}}\n117|\tif _, err := r.Resolve(idA); !errors.Is(err, ErrUnavailable) {\n118|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"nil learned index: %v\", err)\n119|\t}\n120|\tr.Peers = []PeerIndex{{hostA, nil}, {hostA, peer}}\n121|\tif _, err := r.Resolve(idA); !errors.Is(err, ErrUnavailable) {\n122|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"duplicate learned index: %v\", err)\n123|\t}\n124|\tif err := os.RemoveAll(filepath.Join(root, \"sessions\")); err != nil {\n125|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n126|\t}\n127|\tif _, err := r.List(); !errors.Is(err, sessrepo.ErrRepositoryPath) {\n128|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"missing local root: %v\", err)\n129|\t}\n130|\tif _, err := r.Resolve(\"Local\"); !errors.Is(err, sessrepo.ErrRepositoryPath) {\n131|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"missing root became not found: %v\", err)\n132|\t}\n133|}\n134|\n135|func TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity(t *testing.T) {\n136|\tlocal, _ := repository(t)\n137|\ta, _ := repository(t)\n138|\tb, _ := repository(t)\n139|\tcreate(t, a, idA, \"Shared\")\n140|\tcreate(t, b, idA, \"Shared\")\n141|\tr := &Reader{Local: local, AllowlistedPeerIDs: []string{hostB, hostA, hostB}, Peers: []PeerIndex{{hostB, b}, {hostA, a}}}\n142|\tfirst, err := r.Resolve(\"Shared\")\n143|\tif err != nil || first.PeerHostID != hostA {\n144|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"replicated identity: %+v %v\", first, err)\n145|\t}\n146|\tr.Peers[0], r.Peers[1] = r.Peers[1], r.Peers[0]\n147|\tsecond, err := r.Resolve(\"Shared\")\n148|\tif err != nil || !reflect.DeepEqual(first, second) {\n149|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"permutation changed selection: %+v %v\", second, err)\n150|\t}\n151|\tcreate(t, b, idB, \"sHARED\")\n152|\tif _, err := r.Resolve(\"Shared\"); !errors.Is(err, ErrAmbiguous) {\n153|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"cross-peer collision: %v\", err)\n154|\t}\n155|}\n156|\n157|func TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder(t *testing.T) {\n158|\trepo, _ := repository(t)\n159|\tcreate(t, repo, idB, \"Zed\")\n160|\tref := create(t, repo, idA, \"Alpha\")\n161|\tappendEvent(t, repo, idA, ref.RecordID, \"session.created\", 1, map[string]any{\"session_record_id\": ref.RecordID, \"bootstrap_operation_id\": hostA, \"first_checkpoint_operation_id\": hostB})\n162|\tr := &Reader{Local: repo, LocalHostID: hostA}\n163|\tlist, err := r.List()\n164|\tif err != nil || len(list) != 2 {\n165|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"List: %+v %v\", list, err)\n166|\t}\n167|\tif list[0].Projection.SessionID != idA || list[1].Projection.SessionID != idB {\n168|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"order: %+v\", list)\n169|\t}\n170|\tp := list[0].Projection\n171|\tif p.Name != \"Alpha\" || p.Kind != \"direct\" || p.Provider.ID != \"codex\" || p.State != sessstate.StateCreating || p.OwnerHostID != hostA || p.LocalRole != \"owner\" || p.Winner.LeaseID != lease || p.Winner.Epoch != 1 {\n172|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"derived summary: %+v\", p)\n173|\t}\n174|\tunknown := list[1].Projection\n175|\tif unknown.OwnerHostID != \"\" || unknown.LocalRole != \"\" || !unknown.Winner.IsZero() {\n176|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"invented unknown owner: %+v\", unknown)\n177|\t}\n178|\tfor _, selector := range []string{\"Alpha\", idA} {\n179|\t\tstatus, err := r.Status(selector)\n180|\t\tif err != nil || !reflect.DeepEqual(status, list[0]) {\n181|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"status disagrees: %+v %v\", status, err)\n182|\t\t}\n183|\t}\n184|\tagain, err := r.List()\n185|\tif err != nil || !reflect.DeepEqual(list, again) {\n186|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"read is not idempotent: %+v %v\", again, err)\n187|\t}\n188|\tr.LocalHostID = hostB\n189|\tstatus, err := r.Status(idA)\n190|\tif err != nil || status.Projection.LocalRole != \"replica\" {\n191|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"replica: %+v %v\", status, err)\n192|\t}\n193|}\n194|\n195|func TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed(t *testing.T) {\n196|\trepo, root := repository(t)\n197|\traw := record(t, idA, \"Parked\")\n198|\trepo.AfterCreateStep = func(step sessrepo.CreateStep) error {\n199|\t\tif step == sessrepo.CreateStepRecord {\n200|\t\t\treturn errors.New(\"crash\")\n201|\t\t}\n202|\t\treturn nil\n203|\t}\n204|\tif _, err := repo.CreateSession(raw); err == nil {\n205|\t\tt.Fatal(\"fault did not fire\")\n206|\t}\n207|\tcreateHealthy := func() { repo.AfterCreateStep = nil; create(t, repo, idB, \"Healthy\") }\n208|\tcreateHealthy()\n209|\tr := &Reader{Local: repo}\n210|\tlist, err := r.List()\n211|\tif err != nil || len(list) != 2 || list[0].Projection.Parked == nil {\n212|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parked omitted: %+v %v\", list, err)\n213|\t}\n214|\tif _, err := r.Resolve(\"Parked\"); !errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound) {\n215|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parked routed: %v\", err)\n216|\t}\n217|\tif _, err := r.Resolve(idA); !errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound) {\n218|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parked UUID routed: %v\", err)\n219|\t}\n220|\tif _, err := r.Resolve(\"Healthy\"); err != nil {\n221|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n222|\t}\n223|\tparked, err := r.InspectLocal(idA)\n224|\tif err != nil || parked.Projection.Parked == nil || parked.Projection.Parked.RetryHint == \"\" {\n225|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"parked status: %+v %v\", parked, err)\n226|\t}\n227|\tif _, err := repo.CreateSession(raw); err != nil {\n228|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n229|\t}\n230|\tif _, err := r.Status(\"Parked\"); err != nil {\n231|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n232|\t}\n233|\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, \"sessions\", idA, \"record.json\"), []byte(\"malformed\"), 0600); err != nil {\n234|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n235|\t}\n236|\tdamaged, err := r.InspectLocal(idA)\n237|\tif err != nil || damaged.Projection.State != sessstate.StateParked || damaged.Projection.Parked.BlockingReason == \"\" {\n238|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"malformed treated as absent: %+v %v\", damaged, err)\n239|\t}\n240|\tif _, err := r.InspectLocal(hostA); !errors.Is(err, sessstate.ErrUnknownSession) {\n241|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"missing: %v\", err)\n242|\t}\n243|}\n244|\n245|func TestReaderAbsentAndNil(t *testing.T) {\n246|\tfor _, r := range []*Reader{nil, {}} {\n247|\t\tif _, err := r.List(); !errors.Is(err, ErrUnavailable) {\n248|\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n249|\t\t}\n250|\t\tif _, err := r.InspectLocal(idA); !errors.Is(err, ErrUnavailable) {\n251|\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n252|\t\t}\n253|\t\tif _, err := r.Status(idA); !errors.Is(err, ErrUnavailable) {\n254|\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n255|\t\t}\n256|\t}\n257|\trepo, _ := repository(t)\n258|\trows, err := (&Reader{Local: repo}).List()\n259|\tif err != nil || rows == nil || len(rows) != 0 {\n260|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"empty: %+v %v\", rows, err)\n261|\t}\n262|\tif _, err := (&Reader{Local: repo}).Status(idA); !errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound) {\n263|\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n264|\t}\n265|}\n266|\n267|func TestResolveExcludesTombstonedButListsIt(t *testing.T) {\n268|\trepo, _ := repository(t)\n269|\tref := create(t, repo, idA, \"Deleted\")\n270|\tevent := appendEvent(t, repo, idA, ref.RecordID, \"session.created\", 1, map[string]any{\"session_record_id\": ref.RecordID, \"bootstrap_operation_id\": hostA, \"first_checkpoint_operation_id\": hostB})\n271|\tevent = appendEvent(t, repo, idA, event, \"session.failed\", 2, map[string]any{\"error_code\": \"E_LAUNCH\", \"retryable\": true, \"operation_id\": nil})\n272|\tappendEvent(t, repo, idA, event, \"session.tombstoned\", 3, map[string]any{\"tombstone_id\": zeroDigest})\n273|\tr := &Reader{Local: repo}\n274|\trows, err := r.List()\n275|\tif err != nil || len(rows) != 1 || rows[0].Projection.State != sessstate.StateTombstoned {\n276|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"tombstone lost: %+v %v\", rows, err)\n277|\t}\n278|\tfor _, selector := range []string{\"Deleted\", idA} {\n279|\t\tif _, err := r.Resolve(selector); !errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound) {\n280|\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"tombstone routed: %v\", err)\n281|\t\t}\n282|\t}\n283|}\n284|\n285|func TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure(t *testing.T) {\n286|\trepo, _ := repository(t)\n287|\tref := create(t, repo, idA, \"Checkpointed\")\n288|\tprevious := ref.RecordID\n289|\trows := []struct {\n290|\t\ttyp     string\n291|\t\tpayload map[string]any\n292|\t}{\n293|\t\t{\"session.created\", map[string]any{\"session_record_id\": ref.RecordID, \"bootstrap_operation_id\": hostA, \"first_checkpoint_operation_id\": hostB}},\n294|\t\t{\"provider.launched\", map[string]any{\"provider_id\": \"codex\", \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\", \"execution_profile\": \"yolo\", \"profile_source_event_id\": nil, \"profile_mapping\": \"default\"}},\n295|\t\t{\"session.idle\", map[string]any{\"boundary_ref\": \"turn-1\", \"foreground_idle\": true, \"background_idle\": true}},\n296|\t\t{\"checkpoint.created\", map[string]any{\"checkpoint_id\": zeroDigest, \"kind\": \"manual\"}},\n297|\t\t{\"checkpoint.created\", map[string]any{\"checkpoint_id\": zeroDigest, \"kind\": \"manual\"}},\n298|\t\t{\"session.stopped\", map[string]any{\"graceful\": true, \"checkpoint_id\": zeroDigest, \"resumable\": true, \"closure_kind\": \"checkpointed\", \"process_closed\": true, \"store_closed\": true}},\n299|\t}\n300|\tfor index, row := range rows {\n301|\t\tprevious = appendEvent(t, repo, idA, previous, row.typ, index+1, row.payload)\n302|\t}\n303|\tr := &Reader{Local: repo, LocalHostID: hostA}\n304|\tstatus, err := r.Status(\"Checkpointed\")\n305|\tif err != nil || status.Projection.State != sessstate.StateStopped || !status.Projection.HasCheckpoint || status.Projection.Newest.ID != zeroDigest || status.Projection.Provider.Version != \"0.147.0\" {\n306|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"checkpoint summary: %+v %v\", status, err)\n307|\t}\n308|\tlist, err := r.List()\n309|\tif err != nil || len(list) != 1 || !reflect.DeepEqual(list[0], status) {\n310|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"checkpoint list/status disagreement: %+v %v\", list, err)\n311|\t}\n312|\t// Repository continuity admits this event; the state owner's terminal-state\n313|\t// transition gate refuses it. That failure must reach the read entry unchanged.\n314|\tappendEvent(t, repo, idA, previous, \"session.created\", 7, map[string]any{\"session_record_id\": ref.RecordID, \"bootstrap_operation_id\": hostA, \"first_checkpoint_operation_id\": hostB})\n315|\tif _, err := r.List(); err == nil {\n316|\t\tt.Fatal(\"invalid projection was returned as a summary\")\n317|\t}\n318|\tif _, err := r.Status(idA); err == nil || errors.Is(err, ErrNotFound) {\n319|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"invalid projection became absence: %v\", err)\n320|\t}\n321|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4e1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08787-bf24-7b40-897c-97ffe37e976a"},"sequence":203,"recorded_at":1780531400000401,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137"},"call_id":"call_01a0878826b57920a3848bf78318e563","text":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk: bounded implementation evidence\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.5.0,\n4|commit `28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`, embedded document SHA-256\n5|`562546d240f0fa3e71b47e6359a002f9892c0efd97e19eb55917527552ac484a`.\n6|Full task scope remains §2.3, §5.1–5.2, §5.7, §14.4. This file records partial\n7|implementation; it does not change the normative ownership registry or task AC.\n8|\n9|## Acceptance rows\n10|\n11|**2 of 5 AC rows driven in full at the library boundary; 3 of 5 partially driven.**\n12|The five rows are the original task's selector resolution, ambiguity, list\n13|summaries, status summaries, and deterministic sorting, as in its prior stop-line\n14|packet. **0 of 5 rows accepted for public CLI delivery.** Tests remain uncommitted\n15|in the managed Story until the authorized board handoff/checkpoint flow; this\n16|packet cannot satisfy a requirement for committed/accepted test evidence.\n17|\n18|| AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) | Evidence and bound |\n19|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n20|| Selector resolution | `Reader.Resolve`; retained `Repository.Resolve` | `TestResolvePinnedPrecedence`, `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures`, `TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID` | Partial: local exact name, allowlisted learned exact name, UUID and not-found order; qualified syntax/target/precedence unresolved. No attach/resume/chooser implementation or peer transport/authentication claim. |\n21|| Ambiguity | `Reader.Resolve` → `matchName`; `Reader.Status` → `Resolve` | `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions`, `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity` | Driven: local and cross-peer ASCII-fold collisions refuse, one replicated identity is not two sessions, unique case variants do not resolve. Peer indexes and allowlist are trusted upstream inputs; no claim of freshness or identity attestation. |\n22|| List summaries | `Reader.List` → `Repository.ListSessions` → `Projector.Project` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure`, `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed` | Partial: real identity, provider, owner/lease/local role where known, state, newest checkpoint ID, parked reason/retry. Missing §14.4 supplemental observation fields and public rendering remain pending. |\n23|| Status summaries | `Reader.Status` → `Resolve` → `Projector.Project`; `Reader.InspectLocal` | Same list tests; `TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` | Partial: named/UUID healthy status and explicit local parked/tombstoned ID inspection. Closed CLI summary cannot encode unknown ownership. No fabricated host, capability, workspace, process, checkpoint time or sync observations. |\n24|| Stable sorting | `Reader.List`; `Reader.Resolve` → `peerCandidates` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity` | Driven: bytewise session ID order, deterministic bytewise peer-source tie break, permutation/duplicate-peer-allowlist stability. Tie break selects a source index, not an owner, latest state, or mutation route. |\n25|\n26|## Refusal and recovery coverage\n27|\n28|| Gate | Real entry test | Attack |\n29|| --- | --- | --- |\n30|| Folded-name ambiguity | `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions` | N-collision-pair permits exactly two colliding identities. |\n31|| Exact-name admission | Same, plus `TestResolveLocalNameAndUUID` | N-case-variant and N-repository-case-variant admit one non-exact selector. |\n32|| Live eligibility | `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed`, `TestResolveExcludesTombstonedButListsIt` | N-parked-id and N-tombstoned-id admit one excluded identity. |\n33|| Peer allowlist | `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | N-unlisted-peer reads one unlisted identity. This proves filtering of the input allowlist, not authentication of that allowlist. |\n34|| Duplicate learned index | Same | N-duplicate-peer admits duplicates for one host ID. |\n35|| Read failure propagation | Same | N-read-failure-fallback treats repository-path failure as empty. Missing learned index, nil known index, missing root, and non-directory root are separately driven. |\n36|| Projection failure propagation | `TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure` | N-projection-failure-fallback omits one invalid projection. |\n37|\n38|The shipped mutation runner executes the behavioral suites in an isolated source\n39|copy, checks exact replacement count, preserves raw process exits and named failed\n40|tests, then restores and verifies the copied bytes. It has before/after green\n41|controls, a not-applied control, and a compile-failure control. The latter two\n42|prove no behavioral kill. Measured runs and per-mutant tables are attached on the\n43|task, rather than hard-coding a green claim in this file. No source-text gate was\n44|introduced, and this map is not itself an enforcement census.\n45|\n46|The read entry points perform no durable writes. The crash test interrupts the\n47|real repository create after record installation, inspects the parked projection,\n48|retries the byte-identical create through its owner, and observes the healed read.\n49|Repeated lists return identical values. This establishes read idempotency and\n50|composition with existing recovery, not a new crash protocol.\n51|\n52|Additional bounds: reads across multiple `Projector.Project` calls are not an\n53|atomic repository/mesh snapshot; concurrent writers, fresh peer acquisition,\n54|cross-peer lease union and differing replicated views are not measured. The\n55|repository/projector own record/event admission and validation. No new external\n56|provider, filesystem durability, terminal, RPC or CLI capability is attested.\n57|\n58|## Stop-The-Line dependency\n59|\n60|The existing qualified-selector question is unanswered. An approved contract must\n61|name syntax, source-peer versus winning-owner target, and precedence/ambiguity\n62|interaction. No guessed `name@host`, `host/name`, parser flag or qualification\n63|fallback is introduced. Tests with those strings merely exercise unqualified\n64|not-found behavior; they are not qualification fixtures.\n65|\n66|Public summary composition must obtain required facts from their observation\n67|owners. In particular, a valid event-free Session Record projects empty owner,\n68|lease and local role, while the pinned closed CLI SessionSummary mandates all\n69|three. `TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` reproduces that mismatch\n70|through `Reader.List` and `cliresult.New`. Retain unknown facts and the internal\n71|projection until the authoritative public representation/observation integration\n72|is available; do not synthesize a success-shaped owner. This is a concrete bound\n73|on partial summary delivery, not a claim that writing a renderer is impossible.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
