{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c529","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08787-bf24-7b40-897c-97ffe37e976a"},"sequence":239,"recorded_at":1780531400000473,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08788-393e-74e1-832a-47f7398b4c08"},"task_id":"01a08788-393e-74e1-832a-47f7398b4c08","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08788-393e-74e1-832a-47f7398b4c08","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-6-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff origin/main --stat 2>&1 | head -n 40; echo \\\"===\\\"; git diff HEAD -- LOGBOOK.md README.md | head -n 120\",\n  \"description\": \"Check trunk divergence and candidate docs\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \" .../.activity/EPIC-260829-dz9yvx/events.ndjson     |    11 -\\n .../.activity/EPIC-260830-1uwj54/events.ndjson     |   201 -\\n .../.activity/STORY-260908-18woqo/events.ndjson    |    53 -\\n .../.activity/STORY-260909-2uobs6/events.ndjson    |    26 -\\n .../.activity/TASK-260908-2tkufa/events.ndjson     |   280 -\\n .../.activity/TASK-260908-3kvnm2/events.ndjson     |   118 -\\n .../.activity/TASK-260908-eea478/events.ndjson     |     9 -\\n .../.activity/TASK-260909-3kvql5/events.ndjson     |   191 -\\n ...830-1uwj54_RUN-260907-ad43c8-blocked-audit-2.md |     1 -\\n ...830-1uwj54_RUN-260907-ad43c8-blocked-audit-3.md |     1 -\\n ...260830-1uwj54_RUN-260907-ad43c8-continuation.md |    30 -\\n ...EPIC-260830-1uwj54_RUN-260907-ad43c8-routing.md |     1 -\\n ...830-1uwj54_RUN-260908-0dbb0d-blocked-audit-2.md |     9 -\\n ...830-1uwj54_RUN-260908-0dbb0d-blocked-audit-3.md |    22 -\\n ...IC-260830-1uwj54_RUN-260908-0dbb0d-stop-line.md |    72 -\\n ...IC-260830-1uwj54_RUN-260908-6cfae8-stop-line.md |    58 -\\n ...30-1uwj54_approved-contract-execution-260908.md |     1 -\\n ...60830-1uwj54_approved-contract-resume-260908.md |    17 -\\n ...C-260830-1uwj54_orchestration-handoff-260908.md |    29 -\\n ...EPIC-260830-1uwj54_primary-blocked-audit-3.json |    23 -\\n ...C-260830-1uwj54_primary-owner-recovery-audit.md |     3 -\\n .../EPIC-260830-1uwj54_runtime-install.tar.gz      |   Bin 2116 -> 0 bytes\\n .../EPIC-260830-1uwj54_source-ci-0137.json         |   190 -\\n .../EPIC-260830-1uwj54_source-ci-followup.md       |     1 -\\n .../EPIC-260830-1uwj54_source-landing-audit.md     |    11 -\\n ...yst--orchestrator--codex-_RUN-260907-ad43c8.log |    20 -\\n ...yst--orchestrator--codex-_RUN-260908-0dbb0d.log |    21 -\\n ...yst--orchestrator--codex-_RUN-260908-6cfae8.log |     0\\n ...60908-2tkufa_change-request_rev1-validation.log |   849 -\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_change-request_rev1.patch   | 24819 ------------------\\n ...60908-2tkufa_change-request_rev2-validation.log |   640 -\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_change-request_rev2.patch   | 25070 -------------------\\n ...8-2tkufa_control-config-review-restoration.json |     5 -\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_evidence.tar.gz             |   Bin 561048 -> 0 bytes\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_integration-outcome.md      |    93 -\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_ownership.md                |    52 -\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-implementation.md   |    11 -\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-integration.md      |    13 -\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-recovery.md         |    11 -\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-review-rev2.md      |    21 -\\n===\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex f788b3a..ce98f22 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -1258,3 +1258,24 @@ assertion here rather than a brittle one.\\n - FIX (N1): `TestLoadRefusesSubstitutedFirstEventBlob` (single-event chain, position 0) kills `&& position > 0` while the two-event swap stays green (N16 + precision control). NOTE (N2): bad-member vectors pin the sentinel at the entry but are subsumed by `canonicaljson` one arm earlier — stated in test comments + outcome, not patched.\\n - EVIDENCE: battery 30 applied / 30 killed / 0 survivors (16 narrowing incl N13–N16, 10 arm-deletion, 2 census-only, 2 audit-only; NOT_APPLIED + COMPILE_FAIL distinct); `go test ./...` 24/24 green, `-race` green in 4 groups (all 24 pkgs), vet + GOOS=windows vet/build + gofmt clean, tracecheck 60/98, sessrepo cover 87.2%. Tree `93d4a106fd15cdb335539c2612d3ed84d70f919a` (detached-index write-tree over README + 7 sessrepo files). Outcome + battery log attached as `TASK-260830-wbpf1v_outcome-rev3.md` / `TASK-260830-wbpf1v_mutation-battery-rev3.log`.\\n - SCOPE: `README.md`, `internal/sessrepo/{sessrepo,store,doc,sessrepo_test,crash_test}.go` + `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). Work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n+\\n+\\n+### TASK-260830-21gygk — decision-independent read implementation, RUN-260908-00dda9\\n+\\n+- Added `sessquery.Reader` over real persisted repositories and the accepted\\n+  state projector: local/allowlisted learned-name/UUID precedence, ASCII-fold\\n+  ambiguity, read summaries, deterministic ID ordering and parked inspection.\\n+- Corrected the predecessor local `Repository.Resolve` case-variant admission:\\n+  §2.3 mandates an exact name; ASCII folding governs uniqueness. Its old positive\\n+  case-variant test defended a broader behavior and now requires not-found.\\n+- No qualified grammar chosen. Full task scope is unchanged and its pending\\n+  product question remains unanswered. Public list/status rendering also needs\\n+  observation facts that the accepted state projection does not carry. The\\n+  creating-session/closed-CLI mismatch is reproduced in a named boundary test;\\n+  a fake owner or observation default is not a valid solution.\\n+- Peer authentication, freshness and mesh union remain upstream boundaries.\\n+  The read API accepts learned indexes and a separate configuration allowlist;\\n+  it does not claim these caller inputs are independently attested.\\n+- Managed Story history and accepted predecessor checkpoints preserved. Source\\n+  and validation evidence are attached under TASK-260830-21gygk names before\\n+  lifecycle end; this partial work is not a review or acceptance claim.\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex 84743bf..ffa2342 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -1818,6 +1818,49 @@ on the normal package suite and adds compiler/subprocess time. Task validation\\n logs and mutation artifacts are attached to `TASK-260830-1r9wrr`; scratch\\n outputs live under `.temp/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/`.\\n \\n+## Session name resolution and local read summaries (partial)\\n+\\n+`internal/sessquery.Reader.Resolve` composes the persisted session repositories\\n+and the accepted state projector. It follows v0.5.0 §2.3: exact local live name,\\n+exact live name in allowlisted learned peer indexes, exact UUID, then not found.\\n+ASCII folding detects collisions; a unique case variant is not an exact match.\\n+`Repository.Resolve` now applies that same exact-name rule to its local tier.\\n+Peer source IDs are distinct from winning owner IDs. Duplicate observations of\\n+one session ID do not create a name ambiguity. Peer-source ties use bytewise host\\n+ID order; distinct folded-name session IDs refuse with `name_ambiguous`.\\n+\\n+`Reader.List` and `Reader.Status` read actual Session Records and event chains\\n+through `sessrepo` and `sessstate.Projector`. They expose the derived identity,\\n+provider, lifecycle, winning lease/owner, local role, checkpoint ID, conflicts,\\n+and warnings as an internal `Summary`. List order is bytewise session ID;\\n+`InspectLocal` retains access to parked/tombstoned IDs and recovery diagnostics.\\n+Failed index reads and failed projections propagate as errors. Repository-parked sessions\\n+remain visible in listing but are excluded from live routing. Reading never\\n+repairs a store or performs an attach, resume, or ownership change.\\n+\\n+These entries do not provide an `ax` executable or a closed CLI Result renderer.\\n+Host display names, checkpoint creation time/age, workspace observations,\\n+capability observations, process liveness and per-peer sync timestamps still\\n+need their observation owners. Unknown ownership stays unknown.\\n+`TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` drives `Reader.List` and the\\n+existing `cliresult.New` to demonstrate that a creating session without owner\\n+facts cannot satisfy the mandatory CLI owner/lease fields. No owner is invented\\n+and no doctor/provider/platform capability is advertised. Peer indexes and the\\n+allowlist are trusted inputs from upstream owners; these entries do not prove\\n+mesh authentication, completeness, freshness, or cross-peer lease union.\\n+\\n+TASK-260830-21gygk remains partial: qualified-selector syntax, target and\\n+precedence await the existing product decision. Unqualified strings containing\\n+`@` or `/` currently follow ordinary not-found matching; those tests are not an\\n+approved qualified-selector contract. The traceability and remaining bounds are\\n+in [the task evidence map](internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md). No additional\\n+normative section is marked implemented by this partial work.\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+go test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo -count=1 -v\\n+python3 internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py /absolute/path/to/new/evidence-dir\\n+```\\n+\\n ## Structured Errors, Stable Codes, and Causal Redaction\\n \\n [`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) implements the Section 15 Structured\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 8390,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2098,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
