one issuance and resolution, and retention of the event and every referenced immutable object for as long as the Session Record. No retention, expiry or garbage-collection rule is implemented.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"internal/localstore/projection.go opens, rebuilds and recovers the SQLite projection a\\n---\\n{\\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.1\\\", \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.1 requires SSH host-channel launch with exclusive TLS 1.3, ALPN ax-host/1 and full mutual certificate authentication; no launcher, TLS endpoint or handshake exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-z1yxg9.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The repository carries no TLS, X.509 or SSH-launch code: provhost speaks the provider-plugin protocol over stdio, secprim checks argv, environment and paths, and the mesh RPC layer is catalog vocabulary without a transpor\\n---\\n{\\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.2\\\", \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.2 requires certificate issuance into a machine-local trust store with enrolled roots and exact leaf checks; no issuance, store or enrollment implementation exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260909-2ez769.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"No certificate, key custody or trust-store code exists: internal/config reads TOML only, internal/localstore keeps blobs and a SQLite projection, and the two new pin fixtures are byte identities without a Go consumer.\\\"}\\n---\\n{\\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.3\\\", \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.3 requires credential rotation, revocation and authorization generations that refuse stale trust; no rotation or revocation implementation exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260909-2ez769.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Nothing in the tree rotates or revokes credentials: there is no credential store to rotate, no revocation list reader, and no authorization-generation check outside the specification text.\\\"}\\n---\\n{\\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.4\\\", \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.4 bounds host-channel assurance and executable fixture conformance; no assurance measurement or host-channel fixture runner exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The pinned host_channel_conformance fixture is a lock identity only: internal/secconftest runs crash, hostile and fuzz harnesses over local surfaces and reads no upstream conformance fixture.\\\"}\\n---\\n{\\\"key\\\": \\\"section:11.10.5\\\", \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.5 defines the upstream public synthetic admission validator, not a runtime requirement to parse SPEC.md during AX host admission. Its source vectors do not establish AX runtime conformance; production host-channel conformance remains pending. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The pinned section explicitly calls the predicates synthetic execution context and separates detailed DER, custody and runtime boundaries from \\n---\\n{\\\"key\\\": \\\"section:14.7.1\\\", \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 14.7.1 requires literal first-at source-qualified selector grammar with configured source-index resolution; no selector parser or source index exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-21gygk.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"No CLI session commands exist at all: the tree builds no ax binary, sessadapter SourceSelector validates directory-protocol members rather than CLI selectors, and Section 2.3 name precedence is shape validation only.\\\"}\\n---\\n{\\\"key\\\": \\\"section:14.7.2\\\", \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 14.7.2 requires resolve-once fact binding with revalidation before execution; no selection planner or bound-fact store exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-21gygk.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Nothing binds selection facts to execution: there is no selector resolver whose output could go stale, and no plan revalidation reads a source index.\\\"}\\n---\\n{\\\"key\\\": \\\"section:14.7.3\\\", \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 14.7.3 binds the five Structured Error 1.4.0 codes to exits exclusively inside CLI Result 5; no Go mapping carries those codes. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-1i7bqr.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The axerror registry is closed over Structured Error 1.0.0 through 1.3.0 with 109 codes; the 1.4.0 code-to-exit mapping has no implementation and no emitter.\\\"}\\n---\\n{\\\"key\\\": \\\"section:14.7.4\\\", \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 14.7.4 requires interrupted record-only creation with authoritative bootstrap recovery; no chooser, bootstrap creation or recovery flow exists. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-1wb06o.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"No session creation path exists in the tree: there is no CLI create command, no chooser, and no bootstrap lease issuance that an interruption could leave record-only.\\\"}\\n---\\n{\\\"key\\\": \\\"section:14.7.5\\\", \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 14.7.5 defines the upstream selector publication evaluator and its source-only case inventory. Source publication does not attest runtime provenance, temporal boundaries or running AX implementation; product selector conformance remains pending. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-1i7bqr.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The pinned section explicitly distinguishes the publication evaluator from runtime authority/durability obligations. Upstream source publication ow\\n---\\nacceptance cases: 101\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5652,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1413,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
