{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d09f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08787-bf24-7b40-897c-97ffe37e976a"},"sequence":1706,"recorded_at":1780531400003407,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08797-a70d-7ab3-ad75-86d38bf73837"},"task_id":"01a08797-a70d-7ab3-ad75-86d38bf73837","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08797-a70d-7ab3-ad75-86d38bf73837","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-5\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-// Package sessquery composes the session repository and state projector for\n-// read-only NAME/UUID resolution and local list/status summaries. It implements\n-// the specified portions of TASK-260830-21gygk against SPEC v0.5.0 Sections 2.3,\n-// 5.1–5.2, 5.7 and 14.4. It defines no qualified-selector grammar or action route.\n-package sessquery\n+// Package sessquery is the single shared selector API over the session\n+// repository and state projector: read-only selector resolution\n+// (Section 14.7.1 literal grammar over Section 2.3 tiers), local\n+// list/status summaries, and immutable SelectionPlan construction with\n+// current-fact revalidation (Section 14.7.2). CLI and lifecycle callers\n+// own invoking this API at every required boundary; no second resolver\n+// exists. Unknown owner/lease facts and parked diagnostics stay explicit\n+// in Projection: host display names, checkpoint timestamps/age,\n+// workspace state, capabilities, process liveness and sync timestamps\n+// require their respective observation owners and are never inferred\n+// from a record or a successful read.\n+package sessquery\n","final_result":true}}}
