{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000df57","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08787-bf24-7b40-897c-97ffe37e976a"},"sequence":3590,"recorded_at":1780531400007175,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a087a4-1345-7312-bd23-6a378fcc15be"},"task_id":"01a087a4-1345-7312-bd23-6a378fcc15be","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a087a4-1345-7312-bd23-6a378fcc15be","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-64-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"Session name resolution\\\" README.md; sed -n \\\"$(grep -n '## Session name resolution' README.md | cut -d: -f1),+50p\\\" README.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read current README selector section\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"1833:## Session name resolution and local read summaries (partial)\\n## Session name resolution and local read summaries (partial)\\n\\n`internal/sessquery.Reader.Resolve` composes the persisted session repositories\\nand the accepted state projector. It follows v0.5.0 §2.3: exact local live name,\\nexact live name in allowlisted learned peer indexes, exact UUID, then not found.\\nASCII folding detects collisions; a unique case variant is not an exact match.\\n`Repository.Resolve` now applies that same exact-name rule to its local tier.\\nPeer source IDs are distinct from winning owner IDs. Duplicate observations of\\none session ID do not create a name ambiguity. Peer-source ties use bytewise host\\nID order; distinct folded-name session IDs refuse with `name_ambiguous`.\\n\\n`Reader.List` and `Reader.Status` read actual Session Records and event chains\\nthrough `sessrepo` and `sessstate.Projector`. They expose the derived identity,\\nprovider, lifecycle, winning lease/owner, local role, checkpoint ID, conflicts,\\nand warnings as an internal `Summary`. List order is bytewise session ID;\\n`InspectLocal` retains access to parked/tombstoned IDs and recovery diagnostics.\\nFailed index reads and failed projections propagate as errors. Repository-parked sessions\\nremain visible in listing but are excluded from live routing. Reading never\\nrepairs a store or performs an attach, resume, or ownership change.\\n\\nThese entries do not provide an `ax` executable or a closed CLI Result renderer.\\nHost display names, checkpoint creation time/age, workspace observations,\\ncapability observations, process liveness and per-peer sync timestamps still\\nneed their observation owners. Unknown ownership stays unknown.\\n`TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` drives `Reader.List` and the\\nexisting `cliresult.New` to demonstrate that a creating session without owner\\nfacts cannot satisfy the mandatory CLI owner/lease fields. No owner is invented\\nand no doctor/provider/platform capability is advertised. Peer indexes and the\\nallowlist are trusted inputs from upstream owners; these entries do not prove\\nmesh authentication, completeness, freshness, or cross-peer lease union.\\n\\nTASK-260830-21gygk remains partial: qualified-selector syntax, target and\\nprecedence await the existing product decision. Unqualified strings containing\\n`@` or `/` currently follow ordinary not-found matching; those tests are not an\\napproved qualified-selector contract. The traceability and remaining bounds are\\nin [the task evidence map](internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md). No additional\\nnormative section is marked implemented by this partial work.\\n\\n```bash\\ngo test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo -count=1 -v\\npython3 internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py /absolute/path/to/new/evidence-dir\\n```\\n\\n## Structured Errors, Stable Codes, and Causal Redaction\\n\\n[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) implements the Section 15 Structured\\nError contract: the closed versioned failure object, its stable code-to-exit\\nregistry, its retryability rule, its typed diagnostic details, and the redaction\\nthat keeps a local cause off the wire. The package holds no state, opens no\\nfile, starts no process, and mutates nothing durable, so it has no crash or\\nidempotency surface and advertises no provider, platform, backend, or CLI\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3283,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 821,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
