{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e18b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08787-bf24-7b40-897c-97ffe37e976a"},"sequence":3872,"recorded_at":1780531400007739,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"11672cdc-602f-4a3f-b0dc-7d57f3c36137"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a087a6-96d0-7850-b8a0-1e7152856aab"},"task_id":"01a087a6-96d0-7850-b8a0-1e7152856aab","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a087a6-96d0-7850-b8a0-1e7152856aab","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1833-1874\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## Session name resolution and local read summaries (partial)\n-\n-`internal/sessquery.Reader.Resolve` composes the persisted session repositories\n-and the accepted state projector. It follows v0.5.0 §2.3: exact local live name,\n-exact live name in allowlisted learned peer indexes, exact UUID, then not found.\n-ASCII folding detects collisions; a unique case variant is not an exact match.\n-`Repository.Resolve` now applies that same exact-name rule to its local tier.\n-Peer source IDs are distinct from winning owner IDs. Duplicate observations of\n-one session ID do not create a name ambiguity. Peer-source ties use bytewise host\n-ID order; distinct folded-name session IDs refuse with `name_ambiguous`.\n-\n-`Reader.List` and `Reader.Status` read actual Session Records and event chains\n-through `sessrepo` and `sessstate.Projector`. They expose the derived identity,\n-provider, lifecycle, winning lease/owner, local role, checkpoint ID, conflicts,\n-and warnings as an internal `Summary`. List order is bytewise session ID;\n-`InspectLocal` retains access to parked/tombstoned IDs and recovery diagnostics.\n-Failed index reads and failed projections propagate as errors. Repository-parked sessions\n-remain visible in listing but are excluded from live routing. Reading never\n-repairs a store or performs an attach, resume, or ownership change.\n-\n-These entries do not provide an `ax` executable or a closed CLI Result renderer.\n-Host display names, checkpoint creation time/age, workspace observations,\n-capability observations, process liveness and per-peer sync timestamps still\n-need their observation owners. Unknown ownership stays unknown.\n-`TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` drives `Reader.List` and the\n-existing `cliresult.New` to demonstrate that a creating session without owner\n-facts cannot satisfy the mandatory CLI owner/lease fields. No owner is invented\n-and no doctor/provider/platform capability is advertised. Peer indexes and the\n-allowlist are trusted inputs from upstream owners; these entries do not prove\n-mesh authentication, completeness, freshness, or cross-peer lease union.\n-\n-TASK-260830-21gygk remains partial: qualified-selector syntax, target and\n-precedence await the existing product decision. Unqualified strings containing\n-`@` or `/` currently follow ordinary not-found matching; those tests are not an\n-approved qualified-selector contract. The traceability and remaining bounds are\n-in [the task evidence map](internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md). No additional\n-normative section is marked implemented by this partial work.\n-\n-```bash\n-go test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo -count=1 -v\n-python3 internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py /absolute/path/to/new/evidence-dir\n-```\n+## Session selector, read summaries, and selection plans\n+\n+`internal/sessquery` is the single shared selector API over the persisted\n+session repositories and the accepted state projector. It implements the\n+v0.6.0 selector contract (§14.7/§14.7.1, refining §2.3) with shared\n+SelectionPlan construction and revalidation (§14.7.2):\n+\n+- Literal grammar: split at the first `@` only. The key is a NAME, a bare\n+  UUID (name-first precedence kept), or `id:UUID` (bypasses names for the\n+  durable union identity). The source is empty (bare §2.3 tiers), `local`,\n+  `peer:ALIAS` (the entire remaining suffix, literal — spaces, `@`,\n+  Unicode, and `%` included), or `id:HOST_UUID`. No joining, aliasing,\n+  percent-decoding, Unicode normalization, trimming, or alias folding.\n+- Exact source mappings: effective configuration (local host, peer\n+  alias/host mappings, allowlist) is validated first, including exact\n+  alias and host-ID uniqueness; duplicates are `invalid_config`.\n+  Explicit unknown aliases/hosts are `selector_source_not_found`; known\n+  but disallowed peers are `peer_not_allowlisted`. Remote read failures\n+  are `selector_source_read_failed` with the cause preserved; local I/O\n+  keeps its repository error; malformed authority is `integrity_failure`.\n+- No explicit-source fallback: a qualified key resolves in its one\n+  source only. Tier, collision, and tombstone semantics follow §14.7.1:\n+  exact live name then UUID-shaped name within the source, replicated\n+  copies deduplicate only on agreeing record digests (else\n+  `integrity_failure`), distinct colliding names refuse with\n+  `name_ambiguous`, and tombstoned entries stay excluded on\n+  authoritative tombstone evidence while failed reads never count as it.\n+- Immutable plans: `Reader.BuildPlan` binds the literal selector,\n+  session and validated record digest, source host and exact alias,\n+  index and configuration digests, winning lease triple, event-head\n+  authority heads, action, destination, and expectation digest.\n+  `Reader.Revalidate` compares every bound fact in a fixed order at any\n+  boundary in `BoundariesFor`; divergence is `selector_plan_stale`,\n+  revocation is `peer_not_allowlisted`, and reads keep their classes.\n+  Plans authorize read projection only; fencing, commit, and remote\n+  routes belong to the CLI/lifecycle callers that invoke revalidation.\n+\n+`Reader.List` and `Reader.Status` read actual Session Records and event\n+chains through `sessrepo` and `sessstate.Projector`. They expose the\n+derived identity, provider, lifecycle, winning lease/owner, local role,\n+checkpoint ID, conflicts, and warnings as an internal `Summary`. List\n+order is bytewise session ID; `InspectLocal` retains access to\n+parked/tombstoned IDs and recovery diagnostics. Failed index reads and\n+failed projections propagate as errors. Repository-parked sessions\n+remain visible in listing but are excluded from live routing. Reading\n+never repairs a store or performs an attach, resume, or ownership\n+change. A record without any valid lease keeps the accepted internal\n+projection with empty owner/lease facts: creating is a record AND an\n+authoritative initial lease (§5.7/§13.1 step 2), so a record-only chain\n+is an interrupted prefix for the bootstrap-recovery leaf, never a\n+public creating claim and never a placeholder owner.\n+\n+These entries do not provide an `ax` executable or a closed CLI Result\n+renderer. CLI Result 5 with Structured Error 1.4.0, wire exit binding,\n+lease-record objects, observation contracts, transports, peer\n+authentication, and lifecycle effects belong to their owning leaves.\n+`TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` drives `Reader.List`\n+and the existing `cliresult.New` to demonstrate that a creating session\n+without owner facts cannot satisfy the mandatory CLI owner/lease\n+fields. No owner is invented and no doctor/provider/platform capability\n+is advertised. The traceability, gate battery, and remaining bounds are\n+in [the task evidence map](internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md).\n+\n+```bash\n+go test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo -count=1 -v\n+python3 internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py /absolute/path/to/new/evidence-dir\n+```\n","final_result":true}}}
